    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## SCAFFOLD \u2014 documentId/Sheets credential wired, price-source design resolved\nModeled on Beautiful Nature Scenes' Content Calendar Generator (gap-detection) and Tally Sorter (clear+append). Not yet live-tested.\n\nSETUP TODOs before activating:\n1. Connect a Google Sheets credential (documentId is already wired to the real spreadsheet).\n2. Connect a Claude/Anthropic credential for the extraction step (replace `REPLACE_WITH_ANTHROPIC_CREDENTIAL_ID`).\n3. Connect a Brave Search API credential for the search-fallback branch (replace `REPLACE_WITH_SEARCH_API_CREDENTIAL_ID`) \u2014 get a free/paid key at brave.com/search/api.\n4. Optionally start filling in `Catalog.product_url` per item/store (new optional column) \u2014 rows with a URL take the more-reliable known-page branch; rows without one always fall back to search. Not required to activate; an empty Catalog full of blanks just means every item takes the search branch until you fill some in.\n\nOpen Decision #1 (household-ledger-architecture.md \u00a78), resolved 2026-07-31: hybrid \u2014 known product-page URL when Catalog has one ('Has Product URL?' branch), general web search otherwise. Known-URL is materially more reliable (stable page vs. a search result that could be a reseller/wrong variant/stale cache); search fallback trades some accuracy for zero URL-maintenance burden on items you haven't gotten to yet. Costco's online prices are often member-login-gated either way \u2014 a scrape that comes back priceless there is expected, not a bug.\n\nTwo independent branches, both off the same weekly trigger:\nBRANCH A (top): finds stale Catalog items, fetches a price source (known URL or search fallback), extracts via LLM, stages the result in PriceLog as 'pending' rather than trusting it immediately.\nBRANCH B (bottom): promotes PriceLog entries that have sat as 'pending' for the configured hold period with no newer conflicting scrape \u2014 this is the 24-48h freshness gate from CLAUDE.md/architecture.md \u00a75, implemented as a two-step stage-then-promote rather than a bare scrape-and-trust path.\n\nFailure handling: an item that fails extraction validation is logged via a NoOp node for now (see its own note) rather than retried automatically \u2014 matches the existing Webhook Agent's 'acceptable for v1, revisit later' precedent, not a gap unique to this workflow.",
        "height": 620,
        "width": 460
      },
